# 34. Foreign Key Rules

Use foreign keys wherever the relationship is stable and meaningful.

Examples:

Projects.OrganizationId → Organizations.Id

Projects.ManagerId → Users.Id

Tasks.ProjectId → Projects.Id

Tasks.AssigneeId → Users.Id

ProjectMembers.ProjectId → Projects.Id

ProjectMembers.UserId → Users.Id

Timesheets.ProjectId → Projects.Id

Timesheets.TaskId → Tasks.Id

Do not use cascading deletes for important ERP entities.

Prefer:

ON DELETE NO ACTION

and perform explicit business-level deletion/archive logic.

