# 65. Critical design rule

Do not treat the ERP as a Project Management application with additional features.

Treat Project Management as the first module of an ERP platform.

Core concepts such as:

* Organization
* User
* Department
* Role
* Permission
* Document
* Notification
* Audit
* Custom Field

must be reusable by every future module.

Project-specific concepts such as:

* Project
* Task
* Milestone
* Sprint
* Timesheet

must remain inside the Project module.

Future modules should have their own SQL schemas:

core
project
shared
crm
hr
finance
procurement
inventory

Do not tightly couple future modules to Project Management implementation details.
